    </Member>
    <!-- ── Alarm system support ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Stuck: simulation-only — set true via the popup's SIMULATE STUCK toggle so a valve can
         be made to genuinely fail to reach its limit switch (Fail to Open / Fail to Close, C/D).
         TimeoutOpenAlarm/TimeoutCloseAlarm/UnexpMove are LATCHED (stay true once set; cleared
         only by Reset Fault).
         Loss of Position (E) is NOT latched — its own 2s TON (PosLostTmr) IS the alarm condition,
         so it clears the moment the valve stops being idle-with-no-position. -->
    <Member Name="Stuck" Datatype="Array[1..96] of Bool" Remanence="NonRetain" Accessibility="Public">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
    </Member>
    <!-- Simulation-only scaffolding: gates the one-time "assume closed seat" default a freshly
         added valve gets (see FB_ValveLoop). Real OpenFB/ClosedFB will be genuine physical limit
         switch inputs once the real Dynamic I/O Mapper replaces this simulation, at which point
         this member (and the auto-init logic that reads it) should be removed entirely - real
         hardware never needs to guess a starting position. -->
    <Member Name="Initialized" Datatype="Array[1..96] of Bool" Remanence="NonRetain" Accessibility="Public">
